      "body": "<h2>1. Planning the Business Analysis Approach</h2>\n<p>Before scheduling discovery sessions or writing user stories, the BA must define the business analysis plan. Will the project follow a <strong>Plan-Driven (Predictive / Waterfall)</strong> methodology with formal Sign-Off gates, a <strong>Change-Driven (Adaptive / Agile)</strong> methodology with rapid iterative user stories, or a Hybrid delivery model?</p>\n\n<div class='video-container' style='position: relative; padding-bottom: 56.25%; height: 0; overflow: hidden; margin: 24px 0;'>\n  <iframe src='https://www.youtube.com/embed/S0y_Fq0q5kE' title='Business Analysis Planning and Stakeholder Engagement' style='position: absolute; top: 0; left: 0; width: 100%; height: 100%; border:0;' allowfullscreen></iframe>\n</div>\n\n<h2>2. Predictive vs Adaptive BA Comparison</h2>\n<table style='width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; margin: 20px 0;'>\n  <thead>\n    <tr style='background-color: #f1f5f9;'>\n      <th style='padding: 12px; border: 1px solid #cbd5e1; text-align: left;'>Planning Dimension</th>\n      <th style='padding: 12px; border: 1px solid #cbd5e1; text-align: left;'>Plan-Driven (Predictive)</th>\n      <th style='padding: 12px; border: 1px solid #cbd5e1; text-align: left;'>Change-Driven (Adaptive / Agile)</th>\n    </tr>\n  </thead>\n  <tbody>\n    <tr>\n      <td style='padding: 10px; border: 1px solid #cbd5e1;'><strong>Primary Focus</strong></td>\n      <td style='padding: 10px; border: 1px solid #cbd5e1;'>Minimizing upfront risk and formalizing complete scope prior to build.</td>\n      <td style='padding: 10px; border: 1px solid #cbd5e1;'>Rapid value delivery, iterative feedback, and continuous adaptation.</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td style='padding: 10px; border: 1px solid #cbd5e1;'><strong>Documentation Level</strong></td>\n      <td style='padding: 10px; border: 1px solid #cbd5e1;'>Formal Business Requirements Documents (BRD) and traceability matrices.</td>\n      <td style='padding: 10px; border: 1px solid #cbd5e1;'>Epics, user stories in backlogs, acceptance criteria, and living wiki pages.</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td style='padding: 10px; border: 1px solid #cbd5e1;'><strong>Change Approval</strong></td>\n      <td style='padding: 10px; border: 1px solid #cbd5e1;'>Formal Change Control Board (CCB) with impact and budget assessments.</td>\n      <td style='padding: 10px; border: 1px solid #cbd5e1;'>Backlog grooming, Product Owner prioritization at sprint boundaries.</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td style='padding: 10px; border: 1px solid #cbd5e1;'><strong>Ideal Context</strong></td>\n      <td style='padding: 10px; border: 1px solid #cbd5e1;'>Strict regulatory compliance (FDA, aerospace, core banking replacement).</td>\n      <td style='padding: 10px; border: 1px solid #cbd5e1;'>E-commerce, SaaS platforms, greenfield digital product development.</td>\n    </tr>\n  </tbody>\n</table>\n\n<h2>3. Stakeholder Collaboration Planning</h2>\n<p>Identifying stakeholders requires analyzing organizational hierarchy, influence, and impact. A BA develops a <strong>Stakeholder Engagement Plan</strong> outlining:</p>\n<ul>\n  <li>Who are the key decision-makers, subject matter experts (SMEs), and operational end users?</li>\n  <li>What communication channel, workshop frequency, and review cadence matches each group's availability?</li>\n  <li>What governance process resolves contradictory requirements between conflicting business units?</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h2>4. Establishing Information Management Guidelines</h2>\n<p>Define how requirements artifacts will be stored, versioned, tagged, and traced across Jira, Confluence, and enterprise ALM tools, ensuring long-term auditability.</p>"
