      "title": "Requirements Elicitation Techniques: Interviews, Workshops & Observation",
      "summary": "Master elicitation methodologies: conducting structured stakeholder interviews, collaborative JAD workshops, survey design, contextual observation, and mitigating cognitive bias.",
      "readingTimeMinutes": 38,
      "videoUrl": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=0kY-2Qj4b_E",
      "body": "<h2>1. The Art and Science of Elicitation</h2>\n<p>BABOK explicitly uses the term <strong>elicitation</strong> rather than 'requirements gathering'. Requirements do not sit waiting on a tree to be picked; they reside in the minds of busy stakeholders, buried in legacy documentation, or obscured by operational workarounds. Eliciting true needs requires structured psychological probing, active listening, and rigorous validation.</p>\n\n<div class='video-container' style='position: relative; padding-bottom: 56.25%; height: 0; overflow: hidden; margin: 24px 0;'>\n  <iframe src='https://www.youtube.com/embed/0kY-2Qj4b_E' title='Requirements Elicitation Techniques in Practice' style='position: absolute; top: 0; left: 0; width: 100%; height: 100%; border:0;' allowfullscreen></iframe>\n</div>\n\n<h2>2. Core Elicitation Techniques Comparison</h2>\n<table style='width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; margin: 20px 0;'>\n  <thead>\n    <tr style='background-color: #f1f5f9;'>\n      <th style='padding: 12px; border: 1px solid #cbd5e1; text-align: left;'>Technique</th>\n      <th style='padding: 12px; border: 1px solid #cbd5e1; text-align: left;'>When to Use</th>\n      <th style='padding: 12px; border: 1px solid #cbd5e1; text-align: left;'>Primary Advantage</th>\n      <th style='padding: 12px; border: 1px solid #cbd5e1; text-align: left;'>Risk / Limitation</th>\n    </tr>\n  </thead>\n  <tbody>\n    <tr>\n      <td style='padding: 10px; border: 1px solid #cbd5e1;'><strong>Interviews (1-on-1)</strong></td>\n      <td style='padding: 10px; border: 1px solid #cbd5e1;'>Exploring deep subject matter domain knowledge or sensitive political constraints.</td>\n      <td style='padding: 10px; border: 1px solid #cbd5e1;'>Confidential, deep, permits unscripted follow-up probing.</td>\n      <td style='padding: 10px; border: 1px solid #cbd5e1;'>Time-intensive; stakeholders often describe ideal state rather than reality.</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td style='padding: 10px; border: 1px solid #cbd5e1;'><strong>Collaborative Workshops (JAD)</strong></td>\n      <td style='padding: 10px; border: 1px solid #cbd5e1;'>Cross-functional process mapping, resolving conflicting requirements.</td>\n      <td style='padding: 10px; border: 1px solid #cbd5e1;'>Accelerates consensus across business, IT, and operations in parallel.</td>\n      <td style='padding: 10px; border: 1px solid #cbd5e1;'>Risk of groupthink or domination by forceful senior voices.</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td style='padding: 10px; border: 1px solid #cbd5e1;'><strong>Observation (Shadowing)</strong></td>\n      <td style='padding: 10px; border: 1px solid #cbd5e1;'>High-volume operational desk work (call centers, claims processing).</td>\n      <td style='padding: 10px; border: 1px solid #cbd5e1;'>Reveals hidden informal workarounds and unstated tacit knowledge.</td>\n      <td style='padding: 10px; border: 1px solid #cbd5e1;'>Hawthorne Effect: workers alter behavior when watched.</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td style='padding: 10px; border: 1px solid #cbd5e1;'><strong>Surveys & Questionnaires</strong></td>\n      <td style='padding: 10px; border: 1px solid #cbd5e1;'>Gathering quantitative feedback from large dispersed user bases (1,000+).</td>\n      <td style='padding: 10px; border: 1px solid #cbd5e1;'>Scalable, low cost, provides statistical distributions.</td>\n      <td style='padding: 10px; border: 1px solid #cbd5e1;'>Low response rates; cannot clarify ambiguous answers.</td>\n    </tr>\n  </tbody>\n</table>\n\n<h2>3. Framing Effective Elicitation Questions</h2>\n<p>Professional BAs avoid closed yes/no questions (<em>'Do you need reports?'</em>) that elicit superficial affirmative answers. Use the <strong>Open-Ended Funnel Technique</strong>:</p>\n<ol>\n  <li><strong>Broad / Contextual:</strong> <em>'Walk me through what happens when an invoice arrives in your department.'</em></li>\n  <li><strong>Exception / Boundary:</strong> <em>'What exceptions or edge cases cause this process to stop or fail?'</em></li>\n  <li><strong>Impact / Value:</strong> <em>'When an exception occurs, how many hours are spent resolving it, and what is the cost?'</em></li>\n  <li><strong>Confirming / Summary:</strong> <em>'If I understand correctly, your team spends 15 hours weekly manually reconciling currency conversions because the ERP lacks live FX rates?'</em></li>\n</ol>"
